{
  "name": "What to Expect During a Website Audit for AI Search",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Inventory Pages & Queries",
      "text": "We'll start by mapping out your key services, locations, and the questions your customers are actually asking. This involves looking at things like your Google Search Console data and popular Q&A platforms to understand customer intent. This helps us focus the audit where it matters most, making sure we're evaluating content that could realistically be cited by AI.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Technical Crawlability Review",
      "text": "Next, we'll get super technical. We'll check your robots.txt files to ensure AI crawlers like OAI-SearchBot (for ChatGPT) aren't accidentally blocked. We'll also look at your XML sitemaps, canonical tags, redirects, and how your pages render. AI systems prefer clean, low-latency HTML, so this step is crucial for uncovering technical barriers that might be hiding your best content.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Content Accuracy & Schema Validation",
      "text": "This is where we look at your actual content. Is it accurate, original, and does it provide direct answers to potential customer questions? We'll also validate your structured data (JSON-LD schema) to make sure it accurately reflects what's visible on your page. Discrepancies here are a red flag for AI, reducing the likelihood of citation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Performance Data & Remediation List",
      "text": "Finally, we'll dig into your server logs and any available search performance data to confirm issues. You'll get a prioritized list of findings, clearly separating confirmed problems from hypotheses. This list will give you actionable steps to fix technical issues and refine your content, getting you closer to AI visibility. Remember, the goal isn't just an audit; it's a roadmap to being found.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
